## Usage from Kotlin
```kotlin
val res = URL("https://trycloudflare.com.../api/reciters").readText()
val json = JSONObject(res)
json.getJSONArray("reciters").let { arr ->
    for (i in 0 until arr.length()) {
        val r = arr.getJSONObject(i)
        println("${r.getString("name")} -> ${r.getString("id")}")
    }
}
```

## Usage from JavaScript
```javascript
fetch("https://trycloudflare.com.../api/reciters").then(r=>r.json()).then(d =>
  d.reciters.forEach(r => console.log(r.name, r.id))
);
```

## Usage from Python
```python
import urllib.request, json
data = json.loads(urllib.request.urlopen("https://trycloudflare.com.../api/reciters").read())
for r in data["reciters"]:
    print(r["name"], r["id"])
```

